==Services==
Three [[Hillsbrad Apprentice Blacksmith|Apprentice Blacksmiths]] sell assorted weaponry. They are directed by a man named [[Blacksmith Verringtan|Verringtan]]. Two [[Hillsbrad Tailor|Tailors]], vending assorted clothing, inhabit a small house on the far side of the southernmost orchard.

==PvP Significance==
In the spirit of Hillsbrad Foothill's infamous PvP battles, Horde players need to be careful while completing the {{Horde}} [24] [[Battle of Hillsbrad (quest)]] quest. It is a known spot for high level Alliance [[gank]]ing.

==Trivia==
* In the map from the ''World of Warcraft: Game Manual'', the "Hillsbrad Fields" was simply known as "Hillsbrad", just like in ''Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness''.

==Speculation==
===The farms: a family holding?===
Many of the Hillsbrad farmers, footmen and councilors were redheads. This gave rise to the possibility that the Hillsbrad Fields were privately owned and operated perhaps by a large farming family. It could also have been that the Hillsbrad humans had a dominant redhead gene, considering most if not all of the [[Southshore Guard]]s were auburns.

According to {{Horde}} [24] [[Battle of Hillsbrad (quest)]], the landowners were [[Farmer Ray]] and [[Farmer Getz]]. Whether these two farmers were related (brothers, father/son...) is undetermined.

A sharp eye could notice that the Magistrate and his clerk were not redheads or auburns like the rest of the Fields. So if the farms were owned by a family, it was likely that they were subject to some degree of outside authority.

